---

<DocsLayout
  title="Glossary"
  description="A quick definition list for the core terms used across the docs."
>
  <h2>Project</h2>
  <p>
    The top-level file that stores your scenes, displays, effects, reactors,
    and canvas settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Scene</h2>
  <p>
    A container that holds a stack of displays and effects. Scenes are how you
    separate layers of a composition.
  </p>

  <h2>Display</h2>
  <p>
    A visual element rendered in a scene, such as text, an image, a spectrum,
    or a 3D object.
  </p>

  <h2>Effect</h2>
  <p>
    A post-processing filter that changes the rendered output of a scene after
    its displays are drawn.
  </p>

  <h2>Reactor</h2>
  <p>
    A signal source derived from audio or live input that can be bound to a
    numeric property to animate it.
  </p>

  <h2>Binding</h2>
  <p>
    The connection between a reactor and a property such as size, opacity,
    position, intensity, or rotation.
  </p>

  <h2>Stage</h2>
  <p>
    The main preview canvas where the current composition is rendered.
  </p>

  <h2>Player</h2>
  <p>
    The playback controls and waveform area used to audition the track and move
    through time.
  </p>

  <h2>Live mode</h2>
  <p>
    A mode where visuals react to microphone or MIDI input instead of a
    prerecorded audio file.
  </p>

  <h2>Export</h2>
  <p>
    The process of recording the stage to an image or video file.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
